# Red Panda — PRODUCTION build environment contract.
#
# NAMES ONLY. Every value below is supplied by the release owner at build time
# and NONE of them belongs in git. Copy this to `.env` on the build machine (or
# export the variables in CI) and fill it in.
#
# WHY A SEPARATE FILE FROM .env.example: that one documents the LOCAL DEVELOPMENT
# and internal-demo defaults - LAN addresses over plain HTTP, demo flags, the
# bundled catalog. This one is the contract for an artifact that goes to Google
# Play. Reading the wrong one is how a LAN URL ends up in a store build.
#
# NOTHING HERE IS A SECRET, AND NOTHING HERE MAY BECOME ONE. Expo inlines every
# EXPO_PUBLIC_* value into the JavaScript bundle at build time, so all of it
# ships inside the APK and is readable by anyone who unpacks it. Only public
# identifiers belong here - base URLs, OAuth CLIENT ids, ad unit ids. Never an
# API key, a client SECRET, or a token.
#
# Verify with `npm run release:preflight` before building. It reads this same
# environment and refuses a build that is not externally distributable.

# ── REQUIRED ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The production backend origin. MUST be https - Android 9+ refuses cleartext,
# and an http value makes plugins/with-lan-cleartext-demo.js write a
# network_security_config exemption that exists for the internal LAN demo only.
# Absent, every backend call throws ApiError MISSING_BASE_URL and every screen
# shows its error state: the app fails closed, it does not fall back to
# anything. No default is possible; this cannot be guessed.
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=

# Published privacy policy. Google Play requires one in the store listing for
# any app that collects account data or serves ads - Red Panda does both. Also
# what the Profile > Privacy Policy row opens; the row is not rendered without
# it (src/constants/legal.ts, which accepts only absolute https).
EXPO_PUBLIC_PRIVACY_POLICY_URL=

# Published account-deletion request page, reachable WITHOUT installing the app,
# and declared in the Play Data safety form. Load-bearing in the binary too: an
# account with no password cannot use the in-app deletion path (the backend
# requires the current password and fails closed), so this page is the only
# route the app can offer such an account.
EXPO_PUBLIC_ACCOUNT_DELETION_URL=

# AdMob app id, registered against com.spark.redpanda. app.config.js
# substitutes it into the react-native-google-mobile-ads plugin, which bakes it
# into AndroidManifest.xml as com.google.android.gms.ads.APPLICATION_ID. Unset,
# the committed default is Google's SAMPLE publisher - safe (it earns nothing)
# but the preflight blocks it, because a store build must not register under
# Google's sample account. The sample cannot simply be emptied: the SDK's
# MobileAdsInitProvider is a ContentProvider that crashes on launch on an empty
# app id.
EXPO_PUBLIC_ADMOB_ANDROID_APP_ID=

# AdMob interstitial ad unit, from the same AdMob app. Unset,
# src/services/ads/interstitial-adapter.ts serves Google's TEST interstitial -
# a watermarked sample ad shown to real users, earning nothing. Set this and the
# app id together: a build with one and not the other cannot serve a real ad.
EXPO_PUBLIC_ADMOB_INTERSTITIAL_AD_UNIT_ANDROID=

# ── OPTIONAL, BUT DECIDE DELIBERATELY ───────────────────────────────────────

# Published terms of service. Optional for Play. Without it the Profile screen
# simply renders no Terms row.
EXPO_PUBLIC_TERMS_URL=

# Google Sign-In WEB client id - the load-bearing one on every platform, because
# Google mints the ID token against the WEB client and the backend verifies that
# audience. Must come from an OAuth client registered against
# com.spark.redpanda; any client tied to the old com.anonymous.mobileappecc
# package is invalid. Unset, the Google button is NOT RENDERED in a release
# build (src/services/auth/provider-availability.ts) - the method is hidden
# rather than offered and broken.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=

# ── MUST STAY UNSET / FALSE FOR A STORE BUILD ───────────────────────────────
#
# Listed so their absence is a deliberate choice rather than an oversight. Each
# is an independent preflight BLOCKER when set to "true".

# Offline showcase: local login that accepts anything, bundled clips, ads off.
EXPO_PUBLIC_DEMO_MODE=false
# Bundled mock catalog instead of the backend.
EXPO_PUBLIC_USE_MOCK_DATA=false
# Appends the synthetic "QA 16:9 FIXTURE" card to the catalog.
EXPO_PUBLIC_INCLUDE_QA_FIXTURES=false
# WhatsApp OTP sign-in entry point. The backend CANNOT serve this method in
# production (docs/api-contract.md, "Provider activation status"), so leaving it
# false is what keeps a guaranteed-503 dead end out of the app.
EXPO_PUBLIC_WHATSAPP_AUTH_ENABLED=false

# ── LEAVE UNSET FOR ANDROID V1 ──────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# iOS is deferred past V1. Set these only when an iOS release is actually being
# prepared; EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_IOS_URL_SCHEME is read at BUILD time by
# app.config.js and needs a prebuild after it changes.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ADMOB_IOS_APP_ID=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_ADMOB_INTERSTITIAL_AD_UNIT_IOS=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_IOS_URL_SCHEME=

# ── NOT PART OF THE PRODUCTION CONTRACT ─────────────────────────────────────
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_HLS_PLAYBACK_ENABLED  - defaults to HLS ENABLED when unset, which
#   is the production intent. It is a kill switch, not a fallback: setting it to
#   "false" makes every HLS-backed episode resolve to "Video unavailable" with
#   no MP4 to fall back to. Set it only as a deliberate rollback.
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_MEDIA_BASE_URL        - development only, and currently reaching
#   no production code path: `buildMediaUrl` (src/services/media/media-url.ts)
#   has no non-test call site. A production build receives every media URL from
#   the backend. Do not set it.
